Regarding configuration of SSSG switching timers, we also prefer to per BWP because of the misalignment between gNB and UE. We already agreed the codepoint mapping in case 3 and it is not self-contained. Thus, to avoid the misalignment between gNB and UE, we prefer to per BWP regarding configuration of SSSG switching timers. Proposal 3: Support configuration of SSSG switching timers per BWP In previous meeting, four cases have been agreed for PDCCH monitoring adaptation, the only FFS part is Case 5. We already have agreed Case 3 (2 SSSG switching with PDCCH skipping), thus I think the additional UE complexity will not be increased, On the other hands, supporting Case5 will give gNB more flexibility of the PDCCH monitoring adaptation behaviour. Proposal 4: Case5 (3 SSSG switching with PDCCH skipping) should be supported.
